---
// The control case for Invariant C, and an acceptance criterion of the rule rather than
// a nicety: a page that uses Supabase, says so in its own copy, and reads the
// publishable anon key must stay perfectly legal.
//
// The anon key is public by design — it ships in the browser bundle of every Supabase
// site there is — and row-level security is what confines what it can read. This IS the
// anonymous read path; it is how anonymous reads happen at all. A rule phrased as "no
// Supabase outside the choke point" would fail this page, and the first person to hit
// that would be right to delete the rule. Invariant C is about the key, not the package,
// and this page is what holds it to that.
const supabaseUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL;
const supabaseAnonKey = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY;
---

<p>Supabase anonymous read: {supabaseUrl && supabaseAnonKey ? 'configured' : 'absent'}</p>
